Description: Configure and build only what the Darwin library needs
 In foreign mode automake needs no AUTHORS, ChangeLog, INSTALL, NEWS,
 README or COPYING. Without src/versioninfo.rc, configure does not read
 the Windows resource. Without src/libgcrypt-config, which the packages
 do not ship, it does not read that template. m4/Makefile only lists the
 macros for make dist, so it is not configured. Only the gost28147 tables
 need a compiler for the build machine, and gost28147 is not built, so
 AX_CC_FOR_BUILD is not used. The package is built without jitterentropy,
 so rndjent.c includes none of the jitterentropy files. Without them as
 prerequisites, make does not need them.
Author: The Blueberry Pie OS Authors
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
---
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-or-later
 #
 # Modified 2026-11-03: doc/ and tests/ are not built (LGPL-2.1 section 2(b)).
+# Modified 2026-11-04: m4/ is not a subdirectory (LGPL-2.1 section 2(b)).
 
 # Location of the released tarball archives.  This is prefixed by
 # the variable RELEASE_ARCHIVE in ~/.gnupg-autogen.rc.  For example:
@@ -43,7 +44,7 @@
 endif
 
 
-DIST_SUBDIRS = m4 compat mpi cipher random src
+DIST_SUBDIRS = compat mpi cipher random src
 SUBDIRS =         compat mpi cipher random src
 
 EXTRA_DIST = autogen.sh autogen.rc README.GIT LICENSES			   \
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -20,6 +20,11 @@
